pytest-of-*/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
artifacts/
**/_evidence/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
*.user
*.suo
bin/
obj/

# --- .agents/ coordination records ------------------------------------------
# GIT_MULTI_AGENT_WORKFLOW.md makes .agents/tasks/, .agents/handoffs/, and
# .agents/review-log.md the DURABLE coordination system of record between
# Claude (implementer) and Codex (reviewer). They must stay tracked.
#
# The Stop-hook ~/.claude/scripts/codex-review.sh (outside this repo) appends
# a bare `.agents/` line on every run and checks for its literal presence
# with `grep -qx '.agents/'`. Rather than let that hide the durable records,
# we keep the sentinel line the hook wants and immediately re-include
# everything durable beneath it. Order matters: a parent directory has to be
# re-included before its children, and the final two lines re-ignore only the
# ephemeral review-bookkeeping dotfiles the hook itself regenerates.
.agents/
!.agents/
!.agents/tasks/
!.agents/handoffs/
!.agents/review-log.md
.agents/.last-review-hash
.agents/.review-round-count

# Confidentiality boundary (see ARCHITECTURE.md / AGENTS.md): confidential or
# licensed project material only ever lives under knowledge/restricted/ and is
# never committed. registry/*.db is a disposable, rebuildable index (see
# src/noam/registry/index.py), not authoring content.
knowledge/restricted/
registry/*.db
